WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.400
Yesterday's report ended with no thermometer in the room.

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:06.000
Today there are two:

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.800
one in each Geiger counter on saskatchewan.

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:11.600
Twenty-six point eight, and twenty-six point zero.

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:15.600
Both are inside a counter's case, on the same machine.

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:19.600
Neither has been compared with a thermometer in the air.

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:24.400
And a counter can say two things that are not a temperature:

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:26.800
eighty-five point zero, and minus zero.

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:30.400
Both mean its thermometer has no reading to give.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:39.400
With a room temperature to hold, the fleet can be told how many watts to burn.

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:47.000
The first pass on the live fleet read the room at twenty-six point four, against a target of twenty-one.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:50.200
The fleet drew seven hundred and four watts.

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:55.800
The pass said to shed four hundred and forty-six, beginning with columbia's CPU lanes:

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:57.000
about five watts.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.000
And then it did nothing.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:01.000
It was in advise mode.

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:06.800
That is as far as it has gone.

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:10.000
The controller has never changed a real machine.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:12.000
Wake-on-LAN has not been tried.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:20.800
The house's loss for each degree is unknown, so SeaTac's temperature is read and shown, and not yet used in the law.

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:26.800
And the target of twenty-one was set to give the first pass something to say.

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:28.800
Paul has not chosen it.

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:29.200
So:

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:32.000
how many watts does a room want?

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:36.000
How does the fleet get there without throwing work away?

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:39.200
And what must stay in a person's hands?

00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:43.000
Holding the Room.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:48.200
The fleet's watts set by a target, the room's thermometers, and SeaTac's air.

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:52.400
Begin from far away.

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:54.000
There are five territories.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:54.800
The probes:

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:57.600
what reads the room, and the outside.

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:01.200
They feed the controller, one program on the Mac.

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:02.800
Below it, the fleet.

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:11.600
The controller would give it one step at a time, and every watt the fleet draws goes into the room as heat.

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:15.600
In Orrery, two screens set the target and the mode.

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:18.400
And a proof, on a scratch queue:

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:21.200
the only place the controller has acted.

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:24.600
Four borders.

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:27.000
From the probes to the controller:

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:30.200
a median of five minutes, never one sample.

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:32.600
From the controller to the fleet:

00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:35.800
the queue's own commands, one step a pass.

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:38.200
From a person to the controller:

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:40.200
four words, and no others.

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:43.000
And from the fleet to the room:

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:43.400
heat.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:48.000
First, what reads the room.

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:57.400
Each counter's reading arrives every five seconds, and it is not believed one sample at a time.

00:02:57.400 --> 00:03:01.800
The controller takes the median of a probe's last five minutes.

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:05.400
Eighty-five point zero and minus zero are thrown out.

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:10.200
The second counter sent minus zero forty-two times in the first day.

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:17.600
The temperature that is held is the mean of the room probes:

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:18.800
twenty-six point four.

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:26.400
A probe that moves more than three degrees in five minutes is left out of that pass, and named.

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:30.800
With no fresh room probe, the pass does nothing at all.

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:34.600
Now the law:

00:03:34.600 --> 00:03:37.000
how many watts the room wants.

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:42.000
The law starts from the error:

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:44.000
the target less the room.

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:50.800
Each degree asks three hundred watts, so four degrees asks for the whole one point two kilowatts.

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:55.600
A slow integral adds twenty-five watts for each hour a degree stands.

00:03:55.600 --> 00:03:58.800
Within three tenths of a degree, nothing changes.

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:04.200
The second term is for the outside.

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:09.000
A house loses heat by how far it is above the outside:

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:11.000
UA, in watts a degree.

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:13.000
The outside is SeaTac airport's:

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:13.800
nine degrees.

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:15.400
But UA is unknown.

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:21.400
So the outside temperature is read and shown, and not yet used in the law.

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:26.200
How it will be measured comes at the end of this act.

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:30.400
Out comes one number:

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:32.400
the watts the room wants.

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:34.800
The gains are slow on purpose.

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:41.600
The room's time constant is not measured, and a controller faster than the thing it controls oscillates.

00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:44.800
And no step is taken against the room.

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:53.000
The other side of the balance is what the fleet draws at the wall.

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:57.800
Every watt a computer draws leaves it as heat into the room.

00:04:57.800 --> 00:05:02.200
The difference, wanted against drawn, becomes one step on a ladder.

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:11.600
Now the house's side of it, on the first evening with the house's own heating switched off.

00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:13.200
One line of physics:

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:18.400
what the room gets, less what it loses, is how fast it warms.

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:30.400
At half past eight the room read twenty-six, the outside eight, the fleet seven hundred and forty-nine watts, and the room was falling a quarter of a degree an hour.

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:34.400
It is cooling, so it loses more than it gets.

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:36.400
That bounds UA from below:

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:38.800
more than forty-two watts a degree.

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:44.000
And where the room settles is the outside, plus the watts over UA.

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:46.000
What the next days give.

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:48.000
The record is already kept:

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:50.800
the room, the watts, and SeaTac's air.

00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:59.600
Two days with the watts level give the time constant, and how far over the outside the room settles at these watts.

00:05:59.600 --> 00:06:04.400
A step in the fleet's watts, held a day, gives UA itself:

00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:08.400
the watts changed, over the degrees the settled level moved.

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:14.000
Then the heat capacity, the house's other watts, and the controller's gains all follow.

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:16.400
None of that is measured yet.

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:21.800
Then the ladder, and the three modes.

00:06:21.800 --> 00:06:26.200
None of its arrows has been walked on a real machine.

00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:32.400
What becomes of the difference depends on the mode.

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:33.600
Off does nothing.

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:38.400
Advise, the default, works everything out, writes it down, and changes nothing.

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:42.000
Act carries out at most one step a pass.

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:46.000
Against the live fleet, it has run in advise only.

00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:49.800
The first rungs:

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:53.000
a machine's CPU lanes take no new jobs.

00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:58.200
A paused lane finishes the job in hand, so nothing is thrown away.

00:06:58.200 --> 00:06:59.800
On the live ladder:

00:06:59.800 --> 00:07:03.400
columbia five watts, boburner sixty-four, calber sixty-seven, whitewolf seventy-two.

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:09.600
Then a machine's card lane, after its CPU lanes.

00:07:09.600 --> 00:07:12.400
Calber's is a hundred and fifty-one watts.

00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:14.000
The pace is slow:

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:21.200
one step a pass, fifteen minutes between any two changes, thirty before the same machine is touched again.

00:07:21.200 --> 00:07:28.800
The seven lane rungs take at least an hour and a half; with the power rungs, about three hours.

00:07:31.400 --> 00:07:34.200
The last rung powers a machine off.

00:07:34.200 --> 00:07:38.600
It sits behind a second switch, and that switch is off.

00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:43.400
With it off, act pauses and resumes lanes and does nothing else.

00:07:43.400 --> 00:07:48.200
And a machine that carries a room probe is never powered off.

00:07:48.200 --> 00:07:49.800
Today that means saskatchewan.

00:07:52.400 --> 00:07:56.800
When the room is cold the ladder runs the other way.

00:07:56.800 --> 00:07:58.400
Lanes are resumed first.

00:07:58.400 --> 00:08:07.200
Then a machine that was powered off is sent a wake-on-LAN packet, a hundred and two bytes, and given its lanes back.

00:08:07.200 --> 00:08:09.200
It has not been tried.

00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:11.200
No machine's BIOS was read.

00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:17.600
And on whitewolf and boburner, whether the ten gigabit cards wake their machines is not known.

00:08:20.200 --> 00:08:24.200
Here is that first pass, in the plan's own words.

00:08:24.200 --> 00:08:27.400
The fleet draws seven hundred and four watts.

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:27.800
Wanted:

00:08:27.800 --> 00:08:31.800
two hundred and fifty-seven, the least it can shed to.

00:08:31.800 --> 00:08:34.600
The first rung is columbia's CPU lanes.

00:08:34.600 --> 00:08:35.000
Advise:

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:36.200
nothing was done.

00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:39.400
Four things in it are worth a decision.

00:08:39.400 --> 00:08:43.800
The target was set to give the pass something to say.

00:08:43.800 --> 00:08:47.400
The room is read from inside two counters' cases.

00:08:47.400 --> 00:08:54.600
A target meant for the air of a room will ask the fleet to shed everything against that.

00:08:54.600 --> 00:08:58.600
The fleet drew about seven hundred watts, not twelve hundred.

00:08:58.600 --> 00:09:03.000
Without the power switch, its whole range is about five hundred.

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:07.400
And cheapest first sheds columbia's five watts, for almost no heat.

00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:10.800
The proof.

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:16.200
Everything that acts was proved somewhere else:

00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:21.800
on a scratch queue, with fabricated telemetry and a stand-in for the queue's command.

00:09:21.800 --> 00:09:23.800
Sixty claims, and it ends:

00:09:23.800 --> 00:09:24.200
passed.

00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:28.200
It asserts that the live queue's files were not written.

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:35.400
There, a warm room shed in order, from twelve hundred and twenty watts to two hundred and thirty-two.

00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:46.400
With UA at eighty and the outside five degrees colder, four hundred watts more is asked before the room has moved.

00:09:46.400 --> 00:09:50.800
Held eight hours at a limit, the integral stays at nothing.

00:09:50.800 --> 00:09:56.800
And with every rung used and the room still cold, the plan names another computer.

00:09:56.800 --> 00:09:60.000
A line in the plan, and nothing more.

00:10:02.600 --> 00:10:05.800
Then a simulated room, begun at twenty-four degrees.

00:10:05.800 --> 00:10:13.800
With a time constant of six hours, its third day stays within point four five of a degree of twenty-one.

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:16.600
With twenty-four hours, within point one seven.

00:10:16.600 --> 00:10:21.000
With the outside swinging from ten to eighteen, and UA set:

00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:22.200
point five three.

00:10:22.200 --> 00:10:24.200
The same with no feedforward:

00:10:24.200 --> 00:10:25.800
one point three five.

00:10:25.800 --> 00:10:30.200
Once UA is known, the outside more than halves the error.

00:10:30.200 --> 00:10:38.200
But the simulated room has no delay, an ideal thermometer, and watts that fall the moment a lane is paused.

00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:40.600
The house has none of those.

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:44.800
Last, the two screens.

00:10:47.400 --> 00:10:53.400
Both screens run the queue's hearth verb, which passes on four things and no others:

00:10:53.400 --> 00:10:55.400
target, mode, step and status.

00:10:55.400 --> 00:11:02.200
The power switch, the gains, the probes and the machines' addresses are not reachable from a button.

00:11:04.800 --> 00:11:09.600
The Fleet screen's one button turns regulation off, or on to advise.

00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:13.600
Going to act is done only on the Heat screen.

00:11:13.600 --> 00:11:14.800
Now the pictures.

00:11:17.400 --> 00:11:23.800
This is the Heat screen's Hearth panel, with the live plan of the sixteenth, in advise.

00:11:23.800 --> 00:11:28.200
At the top, the target, and three chips for the mode.

00:11:28.200 --> 00:11:30.600
Act asks to be pressed twice.

00:11:30.600 --> 00:11:31.800
Then the room:

00:11:31.800 --> 00:11:34.600
each probe, its reading and its age.

00:11:34.600 --> 00:11:35.800
And the balance:

00:11:35.800 --> 00:11:41.000
the fleet's watts as a bar, with a mark at the watts wanted.

00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:44.600
On the right, the ladder, the next rung marked.

00:11:44.600 --> 00:11:48.600
The power switch shows its state, and has no button.

00:11:51.200 --> 00:11:52.800
And the Fleet screen.

00:11:52.800 --> 00:12:01.200
Above the machines it would pause, one line says the mode, the room, the target, and the watts now and wanted.

00:12:01.200 --> 00:12:02.400
And one button:

00:12:02.400 --> 00:12:05.200
turn regulation off, or on to advise.

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:09.200
Going to act is done only on the Heat screen.

00:12:09.200 --> 00:12:11.600
Both screens were checked as pictures.

00:12:11.600 --> 00:12:13.200
No button was pressed.

00:12:15.800 --> 00:12:19.000
This last picture is not the live fleet.

00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:26.200
It is a made-up plan, in a scratch queue, to show states the fleet has not been in.

00:12:26.200 --> 00:12:29.400
Act in force, and the power switch on.

00:12:29.400 --> 00:12:31.800
One probe suspect, and one stale.

00:12:31.800 --> 00:12:33.000
Four rungs taken.

00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:41.800
And across the top, the line that says every rung is used, the room is still cold, and which machine would help.

00:12:44.400 --> 00:12:47.200
What was done, and what was not.

00:12:47.200 --> 00:12:50.400
Two room probes are read, and SeaTac's air.

00:12:50.400 --> 00:12:52.000
The controller is written.

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:56.400
Sixty claims pass, on a scratch queue and a simulated room.

00:12:56.400 --> 00:12:59.200
One live pass was run, in advise.

00:12:59.200 --> 00:13:02.400
Two screens are in Orrery, checked as pictures.

00:13:02.400 --> 00:13:09.200
The house's loss is bounded from one evening, and the tool that will fit it is written.

00:13:09.200 --> 00:13:12.400
Act has never run against the real queue.

00:13:12.400 --> 00:13:17.200
No lane was paused, no machine powered off, no wake packet sent.

00:13:17.200 --> 00:13:18.400
Wake-on-LAN is untried.

00:13:18.400 --> 00:13:20.000
UA is not measured:

00:13:20.000 --> 00:13:24.400
more than forty-two watts a degree, and no more is known.

00:13:24.400 --> 00:13:27.600
So SeaTac's air is not yet in use.

00:13:27.600 --> 00:13:30.400
The house's time constant is not measured.

00:13:30.400 --> 00:13:33.200
The gains are a guess made slow.

00:13:33.200 --> 00:13:35.200
The controller is not scheduled.

00:13:35.200 --> 00:13:40.800
The target is not Paul's choice, and the probes sit inside two counters' cases.

00:13:40.800 --> 00:13:44.800
The recipes that need root are written, and not run.

00:13:47.400 --> 00:13:49.400
The room is read now.

00:13:49.400 --> 00:13:52.200
No machine has been changed by it.

00:13:52.200 --> 00:13:58.600
The controller works out the watts the room wants, and says which step it would take.

00:13:58.600 --> 00:14:01.800
It has acted only on a scratch queue.

00:14:01.800 --> 00:14:08.200
When it runs on the live fleet, and when act is set, are Paul's to decide.
